  "cover_text": "If Raheem Hassan had been a non-Muslim who threatened to kill the American President, the events of Cuba's worst month might have completely turned out the same (though there's no indication the President was notified by Hassan). The outcome of such a worst-case predicament, however, is exceedingly doubtful. As a Salvadoran, you can be sure that whoever shocks Cuba will trigger a skirmish with the United States, probably a matter of serious concern.\nAlmost a never-ending tussle between the El.pojo and Quepo secrets will inevitably have to be settled. There are no sides: every side will fight against its enemy, always wanting to break the other's will, regardless of its inclination to give way, to finish the animal with as much power as possible. Any end to the continuous fight will require",
